# feat: bare block statement (lexical scope)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STATEMENT-ONLY, form (A), per owner ruling. A bare `{ stmts }` at statement position opens a child
# lexical scope: bindings declared inside die at the closing brace, and the block's region drops on
# exit exactly as an `if`/`loop` arm body's scope does. It does NOT produce a value and is NOT usable
# in expression position (`var r = { … }` stays a parse error — form B, block-as-expression, was
# explicitly rejected). What SAILED:
#   - PARSER: a new `parser::BlockStmt = struct { body: []Statement }` AST node, wired into the
#     `Statement` union. The statement dispatcher (`parse_stmt.tks`) gains an `is_block_stmt_head`
#     branch — a leading `{` at statement position, tested BEFORE the expression-statement fallback
#     (which previously rejected it with `expected an expression`). Unambiguous: a struct literal is
#     led by a type NAME, and a destructure `{ … }` only follows a binding keyword.
#   - CHECKER: a new `checker::TBlockStmt = struct { body: []TStatement }` typed node, typed by
#     `type_block_stmt` via `type_block` in a CHILD env, so inner bindings do not leak the enclosing
#     `env`. Threaded through every exhaustive TStatement walk (typer/spine/escape/residence/borrow/
#     monomorph/consteval/comptime_fold/initanalysis/metrics/warnings/coverage/reachability), mirroring
#     the `TAdoptStmt` arm — EXCEPT the points-to transfer, where a block recurses under the SAME
#     enclosing region (like an `if`/`loop` body), never opening a fresh adopter region.
#   - CODEGEN (C route): `emit_block_region` — the SAME arm/loop-body region emitter (`tk_region_new`
#     … `tk_region_drop`, a plain drop, NOT the adopter's `tk_region_drop_subtree`), so block-local
#     bindings are freed at the closing brace via the ordinary region-drop path (no manual `mem::free`).
#   - The native (LIR) backend honest-stops on a bare block ("block not yet lowered (N2)"), the SAME
#     N2 gap `adopt` carries — the C route is the one this teach lands.
#
# `.tkb` WIRE. A new trailing statement TAG `9` (`TBlockStmt`: body `[]TStatement`) was APPENDED to the
# `write_tstatement`/`read_tstatement` codec and the string-interning collector — nothing shifts, so
# `TKB_EXPR_VERSION`/`TKB_PROGRAM_VERSION` are UNCHANGED (the benign trailing-add case).
#
# ZERO runtime C touched — no new `tk_*` symbol, no `teko_rt.{c,h}` edit; the region prims the block
# reuses (`tk_region_new`/`tk_region_drop`) already existed.
